      "text": "The median of a set is the value that is in the middle when the set is ranked by value. The set $\\{n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15\\}$ has a median of 9, which means that when the set is ranked by value, the fourth number in the set is 9. The fourth number in the set is $n + 9$, so for the median to be 9, we have $\\boxed{n + 9 = 9}$. Solving for n, we get $n = 0$. The set then becomes $\\{0, 5, 6, 9, 15\\}$. The mean of the set is $\\boxed{\\frac{0 + 5 + 6 + 9 + 15}{5} = \\frac{35}{5} = 7}$. The answer is 7",
