      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The median of a set of numbers is the middle value when the set is ordered from least to greatest. Since we have five values, the median is the third value when they are ordered.\n\nWe are given that the median of the set is 9, so we know that the third value in the ordered set is 9. This means that $n+6 = 9$. Solving for $n$, we find that $n = 3$.\n\nNow we can find the mean of the set by adding up all the values and dividing by 5.\n\nThe sum of the values is $3 + 3 + 9 + 9 + 15 = 39$. Dividing by 5, we get $\\frac{39}{5} = \\boxed{\\frac{39}{5}}$.\n\nThe answer is: \\frac{39}{5}",
